SUMMARY:20s & 30s Moore State Park Hike
LOCATION:1 Sawmill Rd\nPaxton\, MA
DESCRIPTION:Sunday\, March 22\, 2026 | 9:30 AM\nhttps://activities.outdoor
 s.org/s/oc-activity/a5UVX0000012iaf2AA/\nJoin the Worcester 20s & 30s on a
  4 to 5 mile hike at Moore State Park in Paxton\, MA. This hike will take 
 us on several trails by a restored sawmill and stone mill foundations alon
 g the banks of Turkey Hill Brook\, along with mouth-dropping rhododendrons
 \, azaleas and mountain laurel (which won't be in bloom but are still impr
 essive). We will hike through hardwood forests of oak\, maple\, and birch 
 and pass by stone walls and several waterfalls. There are a few hills thou
 gh elevation gain is minimal.Participants must bring:Minimum 1 liter of wa
 terSnacks as necessaryLayers as the weather dictates\, including outer she
 llHat\, gloves\, neck gaiter\, depending on the temperatureHiking shoes or
  boots with good treadBackpack to carry gearMicrospikes and/or snowshoes\,
  depending on the weatherBlaze orange (vest\, hat\, etc.) so you will be v
 isible to hunters (Hiking is not allowed on Sundays\, but always good to h
 ave)Confirmed participants can expect an email a few days before the activ
 ity with weather\, meeting location\, and parking details.After the hike\,
  we will stop by somewhere nearby to grab a snack/lunch.
END:VEVENT
